      "message": "It looks like this test (and several others below) is still missing `fixture-\u003eis_initialized \u003d true;` after successfully calling `fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg)`.\n\nBecause the flag remains `false`, `ft98xx_alg_after` skips calling `fingerprint_algorithm_exit(fixture-\u003ealg)`, meaning the teardown logic is still being bypassed for this test.\n\nTests missing this flag update include:\n* `test_init_success_and_version_query`\n* `test_enroll_step_get_feature_failure`\n* `test_enroll_step_algo_step_failure`\n* `test_enroll_step_success_and_progress`\n* `test_full_enrollment_lifecycle`\n* `test_enroll_cancel`\n* `test_match_get_feature_failure`\n* `test_match_success_no_update`\n* `test_match_anti_spoofing_failure`\n* `test_match_success_with_template_update`\n* `test_match_template_update_failure`\n\n**Suggestion:** To avoid repeating `fixture-\u003eis_initialized \u003d true;` manually in every test, consider wrapping the init call in a small fixture helper function that updates the flag automatically on success:\n\n```c\nstatic int fixture_alg_init(struct ft98xx_bio_alg_fixture *fixture)\n{\n\tint res \u003d fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg);\n\tif (res \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\tfixture-\u003eis_initialized \u003d true;\n\t}\n\treturn res;\n}\n```\nThen you can just replace `zassert_ok(fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg));` with `zassert_ok(fixture_alg_init(fixture));` across all tests.",
